      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Constants of e\n\nThe mathematical e constants.\n\n## Definition\n\ne is a mathematical constant - also called the Euler's number. e is a real and irrational number and defined as:\n\n- **e = lim(x→∞) (1 + 1/x)^x = lim(x→∞) (1 + x)^(1/x)**\n- **e ≈ 2.71828 18284 59045 23536 02874 71352 66249 77572 47093**\n- **1/e ≈ 0.36787 94411 71442 32159 55237 70161 46086 74458 11131**\n- **e² ≈ 7.38905 60989 30650 22723 04274 60575 00781 31803 15570**\n- **M = log₁₀(e) ≈ 0.43429 44819 03251 82765 11289 18916 60508 22943 97005**\n- **1/M = ln(10) ≈ 2.30258 50929 94045 68401 79914 54684 36420 76011 01488**\n- **log₁₀(M) ≈ 9.63778 43113 00536 78912 29674**\n\n## Key Properties\n\n**Derivatives of e:**\n- (e^x)' = e^x\n\n**Integrals of e:**\n- ∫ e^x dx = e^x + c\n\n**Base e logarithm:**\n- ln(x) = log_e(x)\n\n**Exponential function:**\n- f(x) = exp(x) = e^x\n\n**Euler's equation:**\n- e^(iθ) = cos(θ) + i sin(θ)"
    },
